Scene summary: Hook: late afternoon in the hemodialysis unit office, the head nurse of the unit has just been asked by the head of nursing for this month's summary of nurses' dialysis training certificates; some may be close to their renewal date and the data are scattered in each nurse's folder. The product does not appear. 9:16 vertical, realistic live-action, shot on a modern smartphone | Primary Video Type: UGC Native (Kabid keperawatan minta data sertifikat dialisis & STR perawat HD; ada yang hampir habis, data tersebar di map masing-masing) + Supporting Format: Product Demo | Handheld medium shots in the small HD unit office in the late afternoon; one close-up of a row of staff files on a shelf (no readable text); Seq 3 single static tripod medium shot at the office desk. REFERENCE PRIORITY: Use DNA Character as the authority for the talent's FACE and BODY identity only (not the outfit). Use DNA Product as the authority for the exact product identity. WARDROBE below overrides any outfit visible in the DNA Character image. CHARACTER LOCK: Use the DNA Character reference ONLY for the talent's face and body identity: exact face shape, jawline, skin tone, eye shape, eyebrows, hair or hijab style, body proportions and distinguishing features. Do NOT copy the outfit from the reference image; the outfit is defined in WARDROBE below. Keep the exact same face and body throughout the sequence. Do not add accessories or name tags not listed in WARDROBE. WARDROBE (OVERRIDES REFERENCE OUTFIT): Dark navy scrub top and trousers, a white short-sleeve undershirt visible at the neckline, black clogs, square black-framed glasses, silver analog watch. No mask on the face, no name tag, no lanyard, no stethoscope. PRODUCT LOCK: Exact Paket Dokumen Inti Unit Hemodialisis 2026 from the DNA Product reference image (the real package mockup uploaded as an ingredient). Navy and teal dominant palette with white accents. It may appear with a navy folder of printed SPO pages, a printed licensing checklist sheet, a printed A4 intradialytic observation sheet (text not readable), and a laptop showing the package's Excel tools (a shift staffing sheet with green and red status cells, and a dashboard with a line chart). Preserve exact product proportions, packaging appearance and visible design details. Do not redesign, simplify, recolor, or rebrand the product. SET & PROPS: Small HD unit office in the late afternoon: a desk with a laptop, grey metal filing cabinets, a shelf of individual staff files in plain colored folders (no readable text), warm side light from a window. No other people. TIMELINE — 10 seconds: 0–2s Hook · medium shot by the file shelf, he turns and looks to the camera. VO (ID, verbatim): "Kabid minta data sertifikat dialisis." Delivery (EN): calm, serious 2–4s Problem · medium shot, he pulls one plain folder from the shelf of staff files. VO (ID, verbatim): "Datanya di map masing-masing perawat." Delivery (EN): honest 4–6s Problem · medium close-up, he flips the folder open, frowning slightly. VO (ID, verbatim): "Ada yang mungkin hampir habis." Delivery (EN): concerned 6–8s Problem · medium shot, he closes the folder and looks at the camera. VO (ID, verbatim): "Saya belum tahu siapa saja." Delivery (EN): honest, a little uneasy 8–10s Beat · medium shot, he sets the folder down on the desk. VO: none. AUDIO: Quiet office ambience, a cabinet drawer closing, distant hospital corridor sounds. Only the talent speaks. Natural Indonesian, conversational, clear pronunciation, no background music. Lighting/mood: realistic natural light matching the set, clean soft contrast, believable Indonesian setting, not glossy, not studio. Camera: follow the camera style above consistently; stable and restrained, no whip pans, no drone, no 360 orbit. Keep product readable whenever it is on screen. Performance: natural facial expression, believable professional UGC, natural eye contact, restrained gestures, no exaggerated acting. Lips clearly synced to each word. Hands: simple, natural, relaxed movements. CLEAN OUTPUT: No subtitles, captions, generated text overlays, watermark, poster layout, storyboard panels, or added graphics. Do not invent product details, claims, prices, ratings, testimonials, certifications, or guarantees. Keep exact talent face, the WARDROBE above, product shape, colors, packaging, box, navy folder, printed sheets, laptop screen, laptop screen content, and visual details consistent with the DNA references.